Software or the official app it was made for, would infringe.

You consent to the copyright holder changing, adapting or leaving out your
contribution, and you will not assert any moral right in it against the
copyright holder or anyone the copyright holder licenses. If someone
infringes the copyright in your contribution as part of the Software or the
official app, you will join or support, at the copyright holder's cost, any
action the copyright holder takes against them.

These rights do not lapse however long they go unused. You give them in
return for the copyright holder reviewing your contribution and for the
rights section 4b gives you.

Sign off every commit of a pull request (git commit -s) to confirm that you
agree to this section. Pull requests whose commits are not signed off may
be refused.

8. Changes to this license

Only the copyright holder may publish a new version of this license. A new
version counts only once the copyright holder has published it in the
official repository's default branch. A change anyone else makes to the
license file, including through a pull request, is not a new version.

A new version that only adds rights applies as soon as it is published. A
new version that takes rights away applies to you once you have been told
about it (for example in the official repository or on the official
website) and have accepted it, or have kept using the Software for 30 days
after being told. It never makes earlier use a breach. If you do not accept
a new version, you must stop using the Software and delete every copy and
build of it that you hold.

9. Termination

Every permission in this license is given on the conditions in sections 3
to 6; any use outside them is not licensed.

If you break any term of this license, every permission it gives you ends
at once and automatically, and getting another copy of the Software does
not give you a new license. You must then stop using the Software and
delete every copy and build of it, original or modified, that you hold.
Sections 2, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 12 and 13 still apply after termination. The
copyright holder may restore your rights by written permission. Ending this
license does not end your right to use the official app, which its own
agreement governs.

